---
# The bookmark icons the Docker role served via its ./icons bind mount — without them the
# bookmark tiles render broken images (E3 audit). binaryData reads the SAME files/ dir in
# the Docker role (single source, like the lookup('template') config keys); ~160KB total,
# well under the 1MiB object limit.
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: homepage-icons
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
binaryData:
{# ONLY the icons a tile actually references — every name here is base64'd into the object,
   so an unused one is dead weight. limitless, LoLalytics, opgg and tftacademy stay in files/
   unreferenced; reviving one is adding its name back to this list. A name listed here and
   missing from files/ fails the RENDER, not the deploy.

   These four are here because dashboard-icons has no icon for them: anilist and metatft
   answer 404 at the CDN under every name tried, and monarch and tacticstools likewise. The
   two logos were fetched from the sites themselves on 2026-09-09 — metatft's only as a
   256x256 PNG embedded in /myicon3.ico, since that site serves its SPA shell at every
   ordinary icon path. Anything the CDN does serve (github, google-maps, gmail, …) is
   referenced by bare name in services.yaml.j2 and must NOT be added here. #}
{% for icon in ['anilist.png', 'metatft.png', 'monarch.png', 'tacticstools.png'] %}
  {{ icon }}: {{ lookup('pipe', 'base64 -w0 ' ~ playbook_dir ~ '/roles/k8s/homepage/files/' ~ icon) }}
{% endfor %}
